# Newline-separated regexes for paths TruffleHog should skip.
#
# The scheduled scan walks HEAD~100..HEAD of git *history*, not the working
# tree, so an inline `trufflehog:ignore` marker only suppresses a finding in
# commits made after the marker was added. It cannot reach back into an older
# commit's diff. Config.test.ts is listed here because commit 9d2d65a added
# the fixture `postgres://user:pass@host/db` without a marker, and that diff
# keeps matching until it falls out of the window on its own.
#
# Scoped to this one file on purpose. The alternative, --results=verified,
# would have been worse: TruffleHog verifies a Postgres hit by connecting to
# it, and a real leaked production URL is unreachable from a CI runner, so it
# would also be reported as unverified. Suppressing unverified results
# globally would therefore hide the exact case this scan exists to catch.
^app/backend/src/infrastructure/config/Config\.test\.ts$
